cvc5 genuinely redirects its regular-output stream to the named file, which is real conforming behavior for :regular-output-channel, but it means the get-option response querying the channel's value right after redirecting is written to that file instead of the pipe jSMTLIB reads, desyncing response/command attribution for the rest of the script -- not observable through jSMTLIB's synchronous pipe-based protocol
